WEBVTT

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:03.120
I didn't want this around the house.

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:03.740
Wait, Tomoharu!

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:05.330
Its build is completely different.

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.830
No matter which existing machine you put it in...

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.230
...this plug-in won't function.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:12.640
Kanade...

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.220
...I'm sure you know.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:15.470
Yes.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:16.670
I know.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.160
Save us...

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.290
Let's make a deal, boy.

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:28.690
W-what?

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:39.010
<i>Asura Cryin'</i>

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:43.350
"Mark of the Cursed Criminal"

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.040
Where is the plug-in?

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.850
Find out as much as you can.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:55.120
Make sure we'll be prepared...

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.660
...if the Asura Cryin' gets it.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:57.910
If?

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.220
You aren't going to...

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:03.200
We have what he wants.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:05.790
We're in control.

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:08.290
But if we go against him...

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.210
It's as Natsume says.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.760
We should give him what he wants.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.020
It's far too dangerous...

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:18.190
...to give a plug-in we know nothing about to the Asura Cryin'.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:21.030
Hundreds of lives are at stake!

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:23.530
She's finally saying something noble.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:24.540
Shut up!

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.320
I can see why you're worried, Kurasawa.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:30.350
No one wants to carry such a heavy liability.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:31.550
Liability?

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:35.930
The Second Student Council is managing their travel insurance.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:37.470
Of course.

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:40.830
If something happens to the hostages, they'll have a lot to pay.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:43.430
So it's money after all.

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.220
But her motive isn't important!

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:48.950
Exactly, Natsume!

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:50.540
We will rescue the hostages.

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:52.540
And we won't give him the igniter.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:53.860
How does that sound?

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:57.120
Why are you so concerned about the igniter?

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:59.290
Is it because you know what it's worth?

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:02.070
Even if I did, I wouldn't tell you.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:05.010
She'd sell it right away.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:08.710
Give me the igniter.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:10.770
I'll call the shots.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.850
You can't dodge bullets from this distance.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.110
Care to test that theory?

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:18.110
Cut it out!

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.080
Hello?

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:24.090
Natsume.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:25.340
Saeki!

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:28.120
Have you heard about the accident?

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:29.040
Accident?

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:33.170
The First Student Council hasn't heard anything.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.920
My brother is on that plane.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.420
What do I do, Natsume?

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:44.270
I'll let you know as soon as we figure things out.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:45.520
Please do.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:47.060
Saeki.

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:51.390
It'll be okay.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:54.750
Reiko.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:56.910
Auntie.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.070
I'll make some tea.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:07.100
Try to work together.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.180
We have to save them.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:20.180
I've never seen Saeki so weak.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:21.670
It'll be fine.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.740
Shuri and Reishiro are on that plane.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.420
I'm sure they can do something.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.830
Did you get it?

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:39.590
Bring it to Ina Port's pier three.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:43.820
Make sure those troublesome girls don't notice.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:45.260
The presidents?

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.040
Hurry, boy.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:50.120
It's not easy for me to keep the hostages alive.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:56.370
Don't give it to him until you're sure everyone is safe.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:57.280
I know.

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:00.930
I'm going to examine the data I collected.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:04.010
We need to figure out what he's planning.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:05.160
Nia.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.260
Don't worry about my sister.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.370
I'm over it.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:15.830
Do everything you can to rescue the hostages, Tomoharu.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:16.790
Right.

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:34.190
This is bad, President!

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.740
Why did you let them go?

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:38.470
They asked me not to say anything.

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:41.640
Can't you have a little more faith in Tomoharu?

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:44.040
If he'll take care of the insurance!

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.830
Mahiwa, get Vivian.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:56.640
Tomo!

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:02.740
Takatsuki.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:08.270
I saw the news and went to your house.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:09.900
You were eavesdropping?

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:10.960
I'm sorry.

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:14.080
I'm sort of relieved.

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:16.200
What do you mean?

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.930
You don't trust us?

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:19.270
That's not what I meant!

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:22.110
And you made her cry this afternoon.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.660
Be careful.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.870
He's using you.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:27.590
Misao!

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.850
That's fine.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.640
I was just kidding.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:35.280
I'm serious.

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:38.450
You promised!

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.450
I...

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:41.720
I have to do it, too.

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:45.080
I have to go.

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:46.910
Please...

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:50.320
But don't worry. I'm not going to fight.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:51.570
I see.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:57.000
Where are they?

00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:58.930
I'll take you to them.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:31.750
So he's stopping time for the entire plane.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:54.100
It seems you're always with that demon.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:55.690
Nevermind that.

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:57.610
Let's get this over with.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:58.520
Ingrid.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:07.370
Release them.

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:09.960
You have the plug-in.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:12.800
This isn't a plug-in.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:16.020
It's the key to straightening out this warped world.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:16.840
What?

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:21.690
I'm sure you've noticed something's not right with the demons and Asura Machina.

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:25.250
Maybe we shouldn't have given it to him.

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:27.070
Hurry up and release them!

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.190
Hold your horses, boy.

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:32.410
This is the second world.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:34.230
What are you saying?

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:39.380
We're being made to play someone's game.

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:41.830
Someone's making fools out of us.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:46.680
That's why I'm going to end this world of suffering with this key.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.180
Don't worry.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:51.540
I'm not like Naotaka Natsume.

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:53.030
My brother?

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:54.040
Tomo!

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.240
What do you mean?

00:07:55.770 --> 00:07:57.500
Naotaka's a good guy...

00:07:57.880 --> 00:07:59.370
...but he failed.

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:01.390
Because of you.

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:06.680
Tomo! Takatsuki!

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:10.670
Don't you want to be free from the constraints of the Asura Machina?

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:12.540
Let them go!

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:15.900
I don't need him to get in my way, too.

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:19.560
I wasn't expecting the Takatsuki girl...

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:22.490
...but this will make things perfect.

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:25.520
Kagakagari.

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:28.780
Looks like you're losing consciousness, boy.

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:31.480
I'll release the hostages.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:33.300
You can sleep well.

00:08:47.910 --> 00:08:48.490
Tomo!

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:54.640
Is that boy that important to you?

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:00.170
Takatsuki!

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:02.910
You're powerless.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:07.380
But you're a hidden menace.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.060
Begone.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:15.840
What?

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:23.190
Vivian!

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:24.390
How did you find us?

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:27.660
President Kitsutaka put a tracking device in the plug-in.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.970
This ends now, Asura Cryin'.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:32.760
To think you had a daughter like that.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:35.350
You've ruined everything.

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:37.350
What a pity.

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:40.490
We'll make you regret making enemies...

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:41.790
...with the Rakurowa Student Council!

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:44.290
Suisho, showdown!

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:05.580
My time stop doesn't work?

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:09.720
The mark of the cursed criminal...

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:12.020
Of course, she's...

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:14.190
...an ex-handler.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:17.550
It must be convenient, being immune to magic.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:18.850
The chains, Kurasawa!

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:21.200
I've got it.

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:22.160
Suisho!

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:25.820
From crystals greater than darkness.

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:28.510
If we can get rid of those chains...

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:30.860
...this plane will move again.

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:33.070
It's over, Asura Cryin'.

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:35.040
We'll see about that.

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:01.380
Toru!

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:02.390
Vivian!

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:06.860
Why you...!

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:11.140
It's pointless.

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:15.510
Suisho!

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:18.250
It's your own fault for getting in our way.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:35.940
What now?

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:45.650
Shuri!

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:48.440
Looks like I owe you one, Kurosaki.

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:51.080
You'll have plenty of time to pay me back.

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:53.080
More obstacles.

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:54.540
Takaya.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:57.760
Kotori's reaching her limit.

00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:16.550
What's going on?

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:24.770
Your foolishness...

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:27.610
...will cost the hostages their lives.

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:35.200
I'll collect the igniter from a mountain of corpses.

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:37.600
Suisho!

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:41.550
Go quickly!

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:45.440
Why weren't you on the plane?

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:48.950
Why don't you ask Honolulu's stupid metal detectors?

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:51.640
I don't even want to know what you tried to get on the plane!

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:00.910
Calm down. There's no need to be alarmed.

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:03.650
Make sure your seat belts are fastened.

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:05.430
What are you doing here?

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:06.630
It's a secret.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:08.750
President Kitsutaka.

00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:10.620
I'm sorry. We made a mistake.

00:13:11.340 --> 00:13:12.110
I heard what happened.

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:14.470
Looks like she burnt herself out.

00:13:16.530 --> 00:13:17.400
I'm sorry.

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:22.640
It's my fault.

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:24.900
No, it was me.

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:27.780
I couldn't do anything.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:29.130
Tomo.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:33.120
Where did you come from?

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:34.220
We'll explain later.

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:37.150
Ask about the plane's condition.

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:42.300
Find somewhere we can land.

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:44.310
We can't stay up here with one engine.

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:45.040
Yes!

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:46.050
Captain!

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:48.050
How are the passengers?

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:49.510
We're barely keeping order.

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:51.040
What's going on?

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:52.870
We're about to stall.

00:13:53.110 --> 00:13:55.470
If we can't find somewhere to land...

00:13:55.470 --> 00:13:56.330
...we'll crash.

00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:58.690
We're running out of time.

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:01.140
We have five minutes.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:13.870
Kotori, are you alright?

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:18.730
The plane?

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:22.810
It doesn't matter.

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:25.840
This world will end in 631 days.

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:30.450
Vivian and I will carry passengers out of the plane.

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:32.470
We'll save as many as we can.

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:33.960
That's all there's left to do.

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:36.940
Get all of them.

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:38.670
Tomo!

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:41.460
I wonder if I can do it.

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:42.950
It'll be fine.

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:44.590
I'm with you.

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:51.170
Do you know where the center of this plane is?

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:52.760
What are you trying to do?

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:56.360
Suisho was able to transform part of the plane...

00:14:56.550 --> 00:14:58.140
...by manipulating magic, right?

00:14:58.380 --> 00:14:59.340
What about it?

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:01.020
I'm going to try it, too.

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:03.190
I'll use Kurogane's control over gravity...

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:04.390
...to carry the plane.

00:15:05.640 --> 00:15:06.740
You can't do that, Tomoharu.

00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:07.750
Don't do it.

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:11.070
There's no way Kurogane can keep that up.

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:13.810
But if we want to get everyone out...

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:15.590
Wait, Tomoharu Natsume!

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:16.980
Why not?

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:18.980
I'm here to save them!

00:15:19.380 --> 00:15:21.110
I don't intend to stop you.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:23.040
What are you talking about, Reishiro?

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:27.310
Aine, how much space do we need to land?

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:29.480
Approximately 2,200 meters.

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:32.890
There is a place ahead to the right.

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:35.680
Captain!

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:37.410
Who are you?

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:39.710
We're going to stop this plane's descent.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:41.300
What are you talking about?

00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:43.990
Come, Tomoharu Natsume.

00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:48.560
There's no need to lift the plane.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.050
But...

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:53.890
I have an idea.

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:56.010
Keep the plane's balance.

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:00.810
Okay.

00:16:01.150 --> 00:16:02.350
Come, Kurogane!

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:07.540
Kurogane.

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:14.510
If I use too much magic...

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:16.290
...I'll destroy the plane.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:19.320
If I don't use enough, it'll do nothing.

00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:22.200
I need to control it.

00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:27.630
What's going on?

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:29.630
We're getting lift.

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:32.440
Looks good.

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:34.550
We're going to land.

00:16:34.980 --> 00:16:36.140
Bring it down.

00:16:36.860 --> 00:16:37.630
Me?

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:39.070
You can do it.

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:42.720
I heard Aine went to you.

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:45.800
That's all I need to trust your abilities.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:52.910
Captain, we're running out of time.

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:54.980
Please listen carefully.

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:59.210
In about 60 seconds, you'll see a ravine on your right.

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:01.030
Take the plane to it.

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:02.000
That's impossible!

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.780
As soon as we turn, we'll stall.

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:06.710
Believe in miracles.

00:17:06.990 --> 00:17:08.440
We got our lift back.

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:10.890
What's in the ravine?

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:14.400
A runway.

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:16.610
Reishiro, you...

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:21.510
Kurosaki, let's fly.

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:31.070
Come on.

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:32.660
Get going.

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:37.850
Bye, Aine.

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:41.310
You go first.

00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:43.040
I'll catch you.

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:44.190
Understood.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:04.530
Tomoharu.

00:20:27.610 --> 00:20:28.760
We did it, Misao!

00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:31.930
I'm tired.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:33.900
I'll take a nap.

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:40.920
President!

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:43.080
Let's go.

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:45.920
We don't need the rescue team to see us.

00:20:46.400 --> 00:20:47.460
How is Takatsuki?

00:20:47.790 --> 00:20:48.660
She's fine.

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:50.660
You must be tired.

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:52.360
Leave it to me.

00:20:52.940 --> 00:20:53.420
Come.

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:54.280
Yes.

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:59.910
I told the students to wait in the plane until help arrives.

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:01.920
It'll take a lot of work to wrap this one up.

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:02.890
Indeed.

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:07.740
President!

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:09.850
President Saeki!

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:13.310
Mr. President!

00:21:15.050 --> 00:21:19.850
The Asura Machina whittle away at their souls...

00:21:20.240 --> 00:21:22.060
...to serve their handlers.

00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:26.390
As their souls are whittled away...

00:21:26.770 --> 00:21:28.390
...their emotions wear away.

00:21:28.840 --> 00:21:32.110
Once they've lost all feeling...

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:34.410
...they disappear.

00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:39.220
Aine's gone.

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:51.860
Aine, thank you for your dedication.

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:56.570
I'm happy I got to be with you.

00:21:57.870 --> 00:22:00.180
You were my moral support.

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:03.350
But you're gone now.

00:22:04.410 --> 00:22:05.510
I know it's true...

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:07.340
...but I can't believe it.

00:22:10.510 --> 00:22:15.080
I hope you'll be able to smile again.

00:22:16.470 --> 00:22:18.390
Good bye, Aine.

00:22:32.380 --> 00:22:33.240
Why?

00:22:37.330 --> 00:22:40.020
Why didn't anyone tell me?
